  "question": {
    "text": "Choose the correct statements about the hydrides of group <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> elements.<br/>A. The stability of the hydrides decreases in the order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>PH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>AsH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>SbH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>BiH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math><br/>B. The reducing ability of the hydrides increases in the order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>PH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>AsH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>SbH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>BiH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math><br/>C. Among the hydrides, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is strong reducing agent while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BiH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is mild reducing agent.<br/>D. The basicity of the hydrides increases in the order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>PH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>AsH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>SbH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>BiH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Choose the most appropriate from the option given below:",
    "image": null
  },
